{"osmosis":{"id":"7842a7fd-487e-4fca-9f0c-6e17bfa666de","word":"osmosis","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"movement of molecules across a membrane","word":"osmose"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"picking up knowledge accidentally","tags":["feminine"],"word":"osmose"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"topics":["chemistry","natural-sciences","physical-sciences"],"categories":["en:Chemistry"],"links":[["chemistry","chemistry"],["net","net#Adjective"],["solvent","solvent"],["molecule","molecule"],["water","water"],["solute","solute"],["concentration","concentration"],["permeable","permeable"],["membrane","membrane"]],"raw_glosses":["(chemistry) The net movement of solvent molecules, usually water, from a region of lower solute concentration to a region of higher solute concentration through a partially permeable membrane."],"glosses":["The net movement of solvent molecules, usually water, from a region of lower solute concentration to a region of higher solute concentration through a partially permeable membrane."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"f54d4560-3d66-4262-8292-4a84f28026d0"},{"examples":[{"text":"Near-synonym: serendipity","id":"8e3ce7c3-f588-4614-8ff2-59745b14ddc5"},{"text":"I was reading about chickens, and I guess I learned about hawks through osmosis.","bold_text_offsets":[[72,79]],"type":"example","id":"67e4808b-6315-458d-b190-3c7ec9e82953"},{"text":"At age fourteen, by a process of osmosis, of dirty jokes, whispered secrets and filthy ballads, Tristram learned of sex.","ref":"1999, Neil Gaiman, Stardust (Perennial paperback), published 2001, pages 36–37:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[33,40]],"id":"cb72be6f-eeb0-4ab0-9a29-60ce57e3c37f"}],"links":[["Passive","passive"],["absorption","absorption"],["impartation","impartation"],["incidentally","incidentally"],["consciously","consciously"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"serendipity"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","E